  "verdict": "Image level (primary, n=9846): PASSED-subset MEL AUROC 0.7872 [0.7586, 0.8155] vs FLAGGED-subset 0.7597 [0.7170, 0.8019] -- a gap of +0.0275. Against the sealed ALL-BCN-test cross-centre AUROC of 0.7962 (what the classifier gets with no gate at all), the PASSED image subset scores -0.0090 -- close to the ungated number, so the gate is not buying much melanoma-detection quality on the images it lets through, whatever its rank-separation AUROC says. Melanoma is flagged LESS often than the other four groups: 29.4% of MEL images vs a 57.2% mean across NEV/BCC/SK/MISC (image level) -- no strong evidence the gate singles out melanoma for downgrade. Coverage sweep (image level, PASSED-subset MEL AUROC as the threshold tightens from p=1 to p=20): [0.7872, 0.7934, 0.7799, 0.7844, 0.7194] -- does not rise monotonically, so the registered p=1 operating point is already close to the ceiling of what this gate can buy; tightening further mostly trades away coverage without a reliable quality return. Post-hoc on the sealed BCN TEST lesions (n=712, post_hoc_bcn_test_reread=true): PASSED MEL AUROC 0.7805 vs FLAGGED 0.6990 -- the same direction as the primary train+valid result above."
}
